<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="FB_AnalogOutput" Id="{005f4470-ef0f-4285-b985-3f15db73e28a}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    FB_AnalogOutput - analog voltage output with limits, ramp and waveform

    Drives one analog output channel, e.g. as the control voltage of a power
    supply or motor controller, in one of two modes:

    Ramp mode (Cfg.Mode 0): the output moves from its present value towards
    Cfg.Setpoint by at most Cfg.VelocityVPerS x cycle time per cycle and
    reaches the setpoint exactly. A setpoint change, also during a ramp,
    continues from the present value without a step.

    Waveform mode (Cfg.Mode 1): an accepted start plays Data[1] to
    Data[WaveformPoints], each for StepTimeMs, and repeats from Data[1] until
    Repeats passes are complete (0 = endless). Then the output holds the last
    element. Without an accepted start, nothing plays, also after a PLC start.
    Waveforms of several outputs started in the same cycle step in lockstep.

    Switching from waveform to ramp mode stops a playback and ramps from the
    present value. Switching to waveform mode holds the present value until a
    start. In every mode the output is clamped to LimitMin..LimitMax last.

    Raw value: Value x 32767 / 10 V (16-bit +/-10 V terminals, e.g. EL4132),
    rounded and clamped to -32768..32767. Other terminals: SetScale().

    I/O (link in the I/O configuration):
        Raw    AT %Q*  INT   channel output value

    Use from ST:
        // optional, once: other terminal scaling
        // Ao1.SetScale(RawFullScale := 32767, ValueFullScale := 10.0);
        // every cycle
        Ao1();
        Acq.Channel[2].Input := Ao1.Status.Value;   // record the output
        // two waveforms in lockstep: start both in the same cycle
        IF StartScan THEN
            StartScan := FALSE;
            AoX.Start();
            AoY.Start();
        END_IF

    Methods (ST):
        Start() : BOOL    same as Cmd.Start; TRUE if accepted
        Stop() : BOOL     same as Cmd.Stop; always accepted
        SetScale(RawFullScale : DINT; ValueFullScale : REAL) : BOOL
                          raw = Value x RawFullScale / ValueFullScale; rejected
                          if either is 0

    Cmd (written by the client, cleared by the block when processed):
        Start   BOOL    start the waveform. Rejected if Cfg.Mode is not 1,
                        while playing, if WaveformPoints is outside
                        1..GVL_Param.AO_WAVEFORM_LENGTH, StepTimeMs <= 0 or
                        Repeats < 0.
        Stop    BOOL    end the playback and hold the present value

    Cfg (written by the client):
        Mode            INT   live; 0 = ramp, 1 = waveform
        Setpoint        REAL  live; V; clamped to the limits, Cfg keeps the
                              written value
        VelocityVPerS   REAL  live; V/s, > 0
        LimitMin        REAL  live; V, <= LimitMax
        LimitMax        REAL  live; V
        WaveformPoints  DINT  at start; 1..GVL_Param.AO_WAVEFORM_LENGTH
        StepTimeMs      REAL  at start; ms per element, > 0, rounded to whole
                              cycles, at least 1
        Repeats         DINT  at start; number of passes, 0 = endless
    An invalid live value (unknown Mode, VelocityVPerS <= 0,
    LimitMin > LimitMax) is reported as an error while it is present; the
    block keeps the last valid value.

    Status (read only):
        State           INT         0 RAMP, 1 WAVEFORM_IDLE, 2 WAVEFORM_PLAYING
                                    (see E_AoState)
        StateText       STRING(20)  name of State
        Error           BOOL        TRUE while a live value is invalid, or
                                    after a rejected command until the next
                                    accepted one
        ErrorText       STRING(80)  e.g. 'Start rejected: Mode is not waveform (1)'
        Value           REAL        V, present output value
        Raw             INT         raw value sent to the terminal
        SetpointReached BOOL        ramp mode: Value equals the limited setpoint
        Limited         BOOL        the setpoint or waveform value is clamped
        Mode            INT         mode in use
        VelocityVPerS   REAL        V/s, velocity in use
        LimitMin        REAL        V, limits in use
        LimitMax        REAL        V
        Index           DINT        waveform: element being output
        RepeatsDone     DINT        waveform: completed passes since the start
        WaveformPoints  DINT        waveform: points of the accepted start
        Repeats         DINT        waveform: repeats of the accepted start
        StepTimeMs      REAL        waveform: ms, effective step time

    Data (written by the client):
        Data            ARRAY[1..GVL_Param.AO_WAVEFORM_LENGTH] OF REAL, V.
                        Writable at any time; a changed element is used from
                        its next output on.

    Waveform upload with TwincatAds (instance MAIN.Ao1, Data configured in
    the device's array_symbols, the Cfg/Cmd/Status members in scalar_symbols):
        1. Write Cfg.Mode = 1. The output holds its present value.
        2. Write the N values with the array write command of MAIN.Ao1.Data,
           starting at index 1.
        3. Write Cfg.WaveformPoints = N, Cfg.StepTimeMs and Cfg.Repeats.
        4. Write Cmd.Start = TRUE and poll until it reads FALSE.
        5. Check Status.Error is FALSE and Status.State is 2 (WAVEFORM_PLAYING).
        6. Follow Status.Index and Status.RepeatsDone; Status.State returns
           to 1 when the playback is complete. Cmd.Stop ends it early.

    Memory: GVL_Param.AO_WAVEFORM_LENGTH x 4 B, 4 MiB per instance with the
    default.
*)
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_AnalogOutput
VAR_INPUT
    Cmd : ST_AoCmd;
    Cfg : ST_AoCfg;
    Data : ARRAY[1..GVL_Param.AO_WAVEFORM_LENGTH] OF REAL;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    Status : ST_AoStatus;
    Raw AT %Q* : INT;
END_VAR
VAR
    State : E_AoState := E_AoState.RAMP;

    // Last valid live parameters.
    Mode : INT := 0;
    Velocity : REAL := 1.0;
    LimitMin : REAL := -10.0;
    LimitMax : REAL := 10.0;

    // Present output value, and the ramp's value in LREAL so that small
    // steps are not lost to REAL resolution.
    Value : REAL;
    RampValue : LREAL;
    // Limited setpoint of the ramp.
    Target : REAL;
    Limited : BOOL;

    // Waveform working values, copied from Cfg at the accepted start.
    WaveformPoints : DINT;
    StepCycles : UDINT;
    Repeats : DINT;
    // Element in output, element value latched at the start of its step,
    // and cycles spent on it.
    Index : DINT := 1;
    OutputIndex : DINT;
    ElementValue : REAL;
    StepCount : UDINT;
    RepeatsDone : DINT;

    // Scaling: ScaleRaw corresponds to ScaleValue.
    ScaleRaw : DINT := 32767;
    ScaleValue : REAL := 10.0;

    // Error of the last rejected command, kept until one is accepted.
    CmdError : BOOL;
    CmdErrorText : STRING(80);
    // Error of an invalid live parameter, empty while all are valid.
    ConditionText : STRING(80);
END_VAR
VAR CONSTANT
    MODE_RAMP : INT := 0;
    MODE_WAVEFORM : INT := 1;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[
// 1. Live parameters, so that a start sees the mode written with it
ApplyLiveConfig();

// 2. Commands
IF Cmd.Stop THEN
    Cmd.Stop := FALSE;
    Stop();
END_IF
IF Cmd.Start THEN
    Cmd.Start := FALSE;
    Start();
END_IF

// 3. Output value
CASE State OF
    E_AoState.RAMP:
        StepRamp();
    E_AoState.WAVEFORM_PLAYING:
        StepWaveform();
END_CASE
ApplyLimitsAndOutput();

// 4. Status
UpdateStatus();
]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
    <Method Name="AddCondition" Id="{0aff1460-2218-41bb-9b51-6ec84b3b7178}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    Records a condition error; the first one of a cycle is reported.
*)
METHOD PRIVATE AddCondition
VAR_INPUT
    Text : STRING(80);
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[
IF ConditionText = '' THEN
    ConditionText := Text;
END_IF
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ApplyLimitsAndOutput" Id="{076592d5-5a9f-4126-aba4-f3f33714402e}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    Clamps Value to the limits, keeps the ramp at the output value, and
    converts Value to the raw output.
*)
METHOD PRIVATE ApplyLimitsAndOutput
VAR
    Unclamped : REAL;
    RawValue : LREAL;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[
Unclamped := Value;
Value := LIMIT(LimitMin, Unclamped, LimitMax);
IF State = E_AoState.RAMP THEN
    Limited := Value <> Unclamped OR Target <> Cfg.Setpoint;
    IF Value <> Unclamped THEN
        RampValue := Value;
    END_IF
ELSE
    Limited := Value <> Unclamped;
    // The ramp follows the output, so that ramp mode continues from here.
    RampValue := Value;
END_IF

RawValue := REAL_TO_LREAL(Value) * DINT_TO_LREAL(ScaleRaw) / REAL_TO_LREAL(ScaleValue);
IF RawValue >= 32767.0 THEN
    Raw := 32767;
ELSIF RawValue <= -32768.0 THEN
    Raw := -32768;
ELSE
    // LREAL_TO_INT rounds to the nearest integer.
    Raw := LREAL_TO_INT(RawValue);
END_IF
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="ApplyLiveConfig" Id="{348e28e8-d25e-4d66-ad86-73b01e757ec1}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    Validates the live parameters. Valid values are taken over, invalid ones
    are reported and the last valid value stays.
*)
METHOD PRIVATE ApplyLiveConfig
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[
ConditionText := '';

IF Cfg.Mode = MODE_RAMP OR Cfg.Mode = MODE_WAVEFORM THEN
    IF Cfg.Mode <> Mode THEN
        Mode := Cfg.Mode;
        IF Mode = MODE_RAMP THEN
            // Stops a playback; the ramp continues from the output value.
            State := E_AoState.RAMP;
        ELSE
            State := E_AoState.WAVEFORM_IDLE;
        END_IF
    END_IF
ELSE
    AddCondition(CONCAT(CONCAT('Mode ', INT_TO_STRING(Cfg.Mode)), ' unknown (0 ramp, 1 waveform)'));
END_IF

IF Cfg.VelocityVPerS > 0.0 THEN
    Velocity := Cfg.VelocityVPerS;
ELSE
    AddCondition('VelocityVPerS must be > 0');
END_IF

IF Cfg.LimitMin <= Cfg.LimitMax THEN
    LimitMin := Cfg.LimitMin;
    LimitMax := Cfg.LimitMax;
ELSE
    AddCondition('LimitMin must be <= LimitMax');
END_IF
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="Reject" Id="{55012354-432e-4e64-92e2-dbd95c7c42e0}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    Reports a rejected command or call. The state does not change.
*)
METHOD PRIVATE Reject
VAR_INPUT
    Text : STRING(80);
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[
CmdError := TRUE;
CmdErrorText := Text;
UpdateStatus();
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="SetScale" Id="{788f4e95-ebce-47de-9472-10f97c0b4109}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    Sets the raw scaling: raw = Value x RawFullScale / ValueFullScale.
    Default: 32767 = 10 V. Rejected if either value is 0. Returns TRUE if
    accepted.
*)
METHOD SetScale : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    RawFullScale : DINT;    // raw value that corresponds to ValueFullScale
    ValueFullScale : REAL;  // V at RawFullScale
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[
IF RawFullScale = 0 OR ValueFullScale = 0.0 THEN
    Reject('SetScale rejected: RawFullScale and ValueFullScale must be <> 0');
    SetScale := FALSE;
    RETURN;
END_IF
ScaleRaw := RawFullScale;
ScaleValue := ValueFullScale;
CmdError := FALSE;
CmdErrorText := '';
UpdateStatus();
SetScale := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="Start" Id="{19932e60-e8b7-4e43-9038-df2ff24ec5b8}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    Starts the waveform playback with the present Cfg; same as Cmd.Start.
    Returns TRUE if accepted. The first element is output in the next block
    call.
*)
METHOD Start : BOOL
VAR
    Text : STRING(80);
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[
Start := FALSE;

IF Mode <> MODE_WAVEFORM THEN
    Reject('Start rejected: Mode is not waveform (1)');
    RETURN;
END_IF
IF State = E_AoState.WAVEFORM_PLAYING THEN
    Reject('Start rejected: waveform playing');
    RETURN;
END_IF
IF Cfg.WaveformPoints < 1 OR DINT_TO_UDINT(Cfg.WaveformPoints) > GVL_Param.AO_WAVEFORM_LENGTH THEN
    Text := CONCAT('Start rejected: WaveformPoints ', DINT_TO_STRING(Cfg.WaveformPoints));
    Text := CONCAT(Text, ' outside 1..');
    Reject(CONCAT(Text, UDINT_TO_STRING(GVL_Param.AO_WAVEFORM_LENGTH)));
    RETURN;
END_IF
IF Cfg.StepTimeMs <= 0.0 THEN
    Reject('Start rejected: StepTimeMs must be > 0');
    RETURN;
END_IF
IF Cfg.Repeats < 0 THEN
    Reject('Start rejected: Repeats must be >= 0');
    RETURN;
END_IF

WaveformPoints := Cfg.WaveformPoints;
Repeats := Cfg.Repeats;
StepCycles := MAX(UDINT#1, F_MsToCycles(TimeMs := Cfg.StepTimeMs));
Status.StepTimeMs := F_CyclesToMs(Cycles := StepCycles);

Index := 1;
OutputIndex := 1;
StepCount := 0;
RepeatsDone := 0;
State := E_AoState.WAVEFORM_PLAYING;

CmdError := FALSE;
CmdErrorText := '';
UpdateStatus();
Start := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="StepRamp" Id="{de677cc8-ae55-4ba1-9d36-97a6e180f3eb}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    Moves the ramp one cycle towards the limited setpoint.
*)
METHOD PRIVATE StepRamp
VAR
    StepSize : LREAL;
    Difference : LREAL;
END_VAR
VAR CONSTANT
    // Tolerance for LREAL rounding of repeated steps, relative to one step.
    STEP_TOLERANCE : LREAL := 1.0E-6;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[
Target := LIMIT(LimitMin, Cfg.Setpoint, LimitMax);
StepSize := REAL_TO_LREAL(Velocity) * UDINT_TO_LREAL(F_GetTaskCycleTime()) / 1.0E7;
Difference := REAL_TO_LREAL(Target) - RampValue;

IF ABS(Difference) <= StepSize * (1.0 + STEP_TOLERANCE) THEN
    RampValue := Target;
ELSIF Difference > 0.0 THEN
    RampValue := RampValue + StepSize;
ELSE
    RampValue := RampValue - StepSize;
END_IF
Value := LREAL_TO_REAL(RampValue);
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="StepWaveform" Id="{b4b79eef-b990-4c0a-b533-df42fd991b84}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    Outputs the present waveform element for one cycle and advances to the
    next element, pass or end of the playback.
*)
METHOD PRIVATE StepWaveform
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[
IF StepCount = 0 THEN
    ElementValue := Data[Index];
END_IF
Value := ElementValue;
OutputIndex := Index;
StepCount := StepCount + 1;

IF StepCount < StepCycles THEN
    RETURN;
END_IF

StepCount := 0;
IF Index < WaveformPoints THEN
    Index := Index + 1;
    RETURN;
END_IF

RepeatsDone := RepeatsDone + 1;
IF Repeats > 0 AND RepeatsDone >= Repeats THEN
    // Playback complete: hold the last element.
    State := E_AoState.WAVEFORM_IDLE;
ELSE
    Index := 1;
END_IF
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="Stop" Id="{43bb2ebc-3487-46ac-ad5f-5c2e21243b46}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    Ends a waveform playback and holds the present value; same as Cmd.Stop.
    Always accepted.
*)
METHOD Stop : BOOL
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[
IF State = E_AoState.WAVEFORM_PLAYING THEN
    State := E_AoState.WAVEFORM_IDLE;
END_IF
CmdError := FALSE;
CmdErrorText := '';
UpdateStatus();
Stop := TRUE;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="UpdateStatus" Id="{02c7e0da-0e58-48e4-8e94-8f2467ece7d8}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[
METHOD PRIVATE UpdateStatus
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[
Status.State := TO_INT(State);
Status.StateText := TO_STRING(State);
IF ConditionText <> '' THEN
    Status.Error := TRUE;
    Status.ErrorText := ConditionText;
ELSE
    Status.Error := CmdError;
    Status.ErrorText := CmdErrorText;
END_IF

Status.Value := Value;
Status.Raw := Raw;
Status.SetpointReached := State = E_AoState.RAMP AND Value = Target;
Status.Limited := Limited;
Status.Mode := Mode;
Status.VelocityVPerS := Velocity;
Status.LimitMin := LimitMin;
Status.LimitMax := LimitMax;
Status.Index := OutputIndex;
Status.RepeatsDone := RepeatsDone;
Status.WaveformPoints := WaveformPoints;
Status.Repeats := Repeats;
]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>